Z||000000||Philphine||09-07-2001||07:16 PM||||minor fender bender (urethane cutter?). first accident i've ever been in. young girl clipped my rear bumper and cut it in a few places right at the corner. since my car is about 4 different colors and the bumper it's self needed a paint job (but in good shape other wise), what do i expect. i don't really want to beat out the insurance co. but i do want to make sure i 'm back to at least were i was in the project. if i can get another bumper and the cost of the repair epoxy (i had filled in the seam where the bumper changes color to give it more of a one piece look) i won't feel to bad.<P> plenty of witnesses (she hit 3 cars) so i'm in the clear. i just don't know what happens in this situation.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>you can't win. you can't break even and you can't get out of the game.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-07-2001||09:17 PM||||Her fault.<BR>The insurance "Co" should replace the bumper!<P>My $.02||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||09-07-2001||11:05 PM||||You gotta put in a claim with her ins. co.  Also, take it to a shop and get an estimate for replacing the bumper and having it painted... even if you will do it yourself.<P>The ins. co. will probably want their man to look at it too.  Then they will offer you a settlement (most likely) since it is clearly their clients fault.  They will probably want to use a used bumper price... so try to talk them up.  They do have movement room (its kinda like buying a new car!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Once you agree on a $$, the cash is yours to do with what you want.  <P>This past winter a car spun out in front of me while driving my dads 87 Coupe.  The Fiero was ok to drive, front end pushed in a little and some cracks in the fenders and hood, but not too bad.  We got a $2000 settlement on it (estimate was about $4000) to total it out (it had 135K miles on it).  For $1900 my father bought an 85 SE 2m6 with 69K miles, and an extra $600 has rebuilt the wrecked 87.  We made out awfully good with the accident!  lol!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||p-did||09-08-2001||01:11 AM||||Sorry to hear that.  Two weeks ago, I had a Dodge van total out the rear end of mine.  I'm gonna need a fastback clip, rear fascia, tail lamp assembly.  I think the body shop went with a new tail lamp assembly, and a used fastback clip and rear fascia.  I'd just have them buy one from the Fiero Store or something.  At least it'd be good.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Jay Olson<BR>(AKA "fropuff")<BR>'86 GT, smashed rear fascia, fastback clip, right tail lamp assembly||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||09-08-2001||07:35 AM||||have her insurance company issue YOU the damage check. DONT tell them your going to fix it yourself though under any circumstances. Just tell them something like your doing other work on it and will be putting of the repair temporarily IF THEY ASK !||||reg||1
Z||000005||Smoooooth GT||09-08-2001||01:07 PM||||I totalled my 87 GT and the *other* ins. co. paid me $5,200.00 for the gt...  FILE THE CLAIM..  GET HIGH EST. FOR IT ALSO.. dang did'nt mean to sceam...lol   Steve<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4.JPG"> ||||reg||1
